        "Content": "• Detached period residence of exceptional architectural and historical significance \r\n\r\n• Listed on the Fingal Register of Protected Structures\r\n\r\n• Arts & Crafts design with strong neo-Gothic detailing throughout\r\n\r\n• Four bedrooms | Three reception rooms | Large kitchen \r\n\r\n• Magnificent barrel and cathedral ceilings upstairs; extra-high ceilings throughout \r\n\r\n• South-facing rear garden with the adjacent church as a unique and beautiful backdrop \r\n\r\n• Natural hardwood timber floors and feature fireplaces throughout \r\n\r\n• Ample private off-street parking \r\n\r\n• A short, pleasant walk to Howth DART station (Dublin city centre in under 30 minutes). \r\n\r\n• Ber Exempt \r\n\r\n• Close to the village \r\n\r\n• Close to the beach\r\n\r\n• Floor area c.243.7M2 (2,622 square feet)"
